# Two optional long-form vignettes kept as nested-frame examples.

label basement_clock:
    scene clock basement with dissolve
    show renpy thinking at left
    play sound gear_click

    r "The basement clock is larger than the plot outline and twice as opinionated."
    r "It insists that every dramatic pause be exactly four and a half ticks long."
    r "RenPy Mouse climbs onto the minute hand with a screwdriver and a piece of cake."
    r "The cake is for morale; the screwdriver is mostly for pointing at suspicious gears."
    r "One brass wheel confesses that it has been rushing the tender scenes."
    r "Another admits it keeps ringing whenever somebody thinks of a sequel."
    r "The mouse loosens one spring, tightens one sentence, and listens again."
    r "For the first time all night, the clock keeps time without trying to direct it."

    return

label .tune_gears:
    play sound gear_click
    show renpy bright at center

    r "At the repair bench, every gear lies in a felt tray with its name written underneath."
    r "RenPy Mouse turns the smallest one and hears a whole paragraph breathe more easily."
    r "He oils the hinge between setup and payoff, careful not to make it too slippery."
    r "A stubborn cog claims it is foreshadowing; the mouse identifies it as lint."
    r "The clock coughs politely while he removes the impostor with tweezers."
    r "When the mechanism starts again, its rhythm leaves generous room for dialogue."
    r "The repaired gears do not move any labels; they only make the scene feel inevitable."
    r "RenPy Mouse pockets the screwdriver and lets the last click fade naturally."

    return
